#
# Example release-hook config for `ck-git-hosting-deploy --all`. This file
# ends in .example and is never read by --all itself -- only a *.conf file
# under this directory is. It uses ck-git-hosting's own release purely as a
# familiar, concrete illustration of the format; do NOT copy this to
# ck-git-hosting.conf to deploy ck-git-hosting itself. ck-git-hosting's own
# deploy already runs automatically as the first step of the same timer
# --all runs as the second step of (see ck-git-hosting-deploy.service), with
# a health check and automatic rollback this generic mechanism does not
# have. Copy this file (renamed, with real values) to deploy YOUR project
# instead -- see "Deploying your own project" in
# docs/operations/05-releases-and-deploy.md.
#
# This directory and every file read from it, including command= below,
# must be owned by root and inaccessible to any other user (mode 0700 or
# tighter); ck-git-hosting-deploy checks this before every run and skips,
# rather than trusts, anything that is not.
#
# Required:
project=ck-git-hosting
asset=packages
tags=v*
# command= must be an absolute path to a command YOU write and secure the
# same way (root-owned, mode 0700 or tighter). It is run as:
#   command <extracted-release-dir> <tag> <project>
# and is responsible for everything from there: installing or deploying
# whatever the release contains, and its own retry or rollback strategy if
# it needs one -- ck-git-hosting-deploy applies none on a hook's behalf.
command=/usr/local/sbin/example-install-command
#
# Optional:
# services=my-app.service
# health_url=http://127.0.0.1:8080/
# timeout_seconds=300
